  "slug": "binary-search",
  "title": "Binary Search",
  "summary": "Probe the middle of a sorted range and discard the half that cannot contain the target.",
  "usage": "How it works\nInput MUST be sorted in ascending order before searching. Maintain inclusive bounds lo and hi; compare a[mid] with the target, then exclude mid when moving a bound. At every step a possible match remains within [lo, hi]. Useful for repeated lookup in sorted arrays. Sorting an unsorted array first costs extra and changes original indices. Returns a zero-based index or -1 when absent.\n\nProperties and prerequisites\nPrecondition: ascending sorted array. Does not modify input. Duplicates: any matching index, not necessarily the first. Empty input returns -1.\n\nComplexity\nTime: O(log n) worst/average; O(1) best. Space: O(1).\n\nExample\nInput: [2, 5, 8, 12, 16, 23, 38]; target = 16. Output: index 4.\n\nTry it\nUse Play/Pause, Previous/Next, the timeline, and playback speed. Answer the prediction checkpoints to continue; feedback reveals the expected answer. Python is the line-synchronized walkthrough; Java is an equivalent complete implementation. Sorting functions accept empty arrays, duplicates, negative values, and already sorted inputs. Java methods belong inside a class; Python functions can be called directly.",
  "category": "Searching",
  "difficulty": "EASY",
  "visualizer": "ARRAY",
  "complexity": {
    "time": "O(log n) worst/average; O(1) best",
    "space": "O(1)"
  },
  "pythonSource": "def binary_search(a, target):\n    lo, hi = 0, len(a) - 1\n    while lo <= hi:\n        mid = lo + (hi - lo) // 2  # Probe the middle of the inclusive range.\n        if a[mid] == target:\n            return mid  # Any matching index is valid when duplicates exist.\n        if a[mid] < target:\n            lo = mid + 1  # Discard the middle and everything to its left.\n        else:\n            hi = mid - 1  # Discard the middle and everything to its right.\n    return -1  # An empty candidate range means the target is absent.\n",
  "javaSource": "static int binarySearch(int[] a, int target) {\n    int lo = 0, hi = a.length - 1;\n    while (lo <= hi) {\n        int mid = lo + (hi - lo) / 2;\n        if (a[mid] == target) return mid;\n        if (a[mid] < target) lo = mid + 1;\n        else hi = mid - 1;\n    }\n    return -1;\n}",
